framework DecisionAnalysis:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain A3B8CandidateReview:
  description |
    Independent review of the exact integrated A3 and B8 Stage candidate and
    its current CI state.

problem P1:
  |
    Decide whether commit 898e6dda5a333eb6e2a73785ff665a3d89418da7 is a
    review-complete integrated A3 and B8 Stage candidate, distinguish candidate
    defects from repository-wide dependency and base-image drift, and identify
    the smallest next action without merging, tagging, deploying, activating
    schema 3, moving a production pointer, or dispatching a provider call.

premise AUTHORITY:
  |
    Accepted ADR-0030 requirement R24 requires deployed and verified historical
    V2 and new V3 reads, migration resume, qualified V3 validation and mixed
    tuple rejection before schema-3 selection or production migration. The
    accepted integrated plan selects one exact reader and Stage smoke candidate,
    keeps the paid A3 smoke opt-in, and leaves merge, tag and Stage dispatch as
    separate effects.

evidence E_REVISION:
  |
    Fresh remote readback on 2026-09-14 found PR 147 open and mergeable with
    head 898e6dda5a333eb6e2a73785ff665a3d89418da7 matching both local HEAD and
    origin/codex/compact-psyche-repair-integration. The branch is 34 commits
    ahead and zero behind origin/main at 1cdf21009dbb8f4099dbb9ca70760320c50be6aa.

evidence E_IMPLEMENTATION:
  |
    Review of the thirteen files changed by 898e6dd found strict storage and
    envelope version dispatch, content-digest and asset-identity checks, separate
    V3 compiler projections, non-current V3 append, V2-current readback,
    zero-request migration resume, opt-in A3 create-and-discard, and cleanup.
    No schema-3 policy activation, current-pointer movement to V3, production
    promotion, or newly added type escape is present in that commit.

evidence E_LOCAL:
  |
    On the exact local HEAD, npm test passed 349 shared, 437 backend, 20
    frontend, 3 deployment and 5 release tests. npm run typecheck, npm run build,
    npm run static and git diff --check passed. npm run adr:check exited zero;
    ADR-0030 and ADR-0031 audited clean, while the previously recorded legacy
    ADR-0015, 0016, 0017 and 0019 findings remained outside this commit.

evidence E_PR_CI:
  |
    GitHub Actions run 34799933363 passed validate and worker but failed security
    and backend-image. The security job reported newly unaccepted advisories for
    hono below 4.13.5 and sharp below 0.35.4. The backend image reported Debian
    libpcre2-8-0 10.42-1 with two HIGH findings fixed by 10.42-1+deb12u1.

evidence E_DRIFT:
  |
    Commit 898e6dd changes neither dependency manifests nor backend/Dockerfile.
    The current lock contains hono 4.12.34, sharp 0.35.2 and wrangler 4.118.0;
    current published fixed versions observed on 2026-09-14 are hono 4.13.7,
    sharp 0.35.4 and wrangler 4.131.1. origin/main CI last passed on 2026-09-08,
    before the 2026-09-14 advisory observations.

premise CAUSAL_CLASSIFICATION:
  |
    For the CI failure, the producing system condition is that repository
    dependency constraints and the runtime image can resolve versions now
    reported vulnerable. The 2026-09-14 advisory and image database state is
    the surfacing condition. The prior successful main run predates those
    observations and is the escape timing, not the defect-producing cause.

premise ALTERNATIVES:
  |
    A record both CI failures as external blockers and leave the candidate
    unchanged; this preserves feature scope but does not yield a green required
    check. B update Hono and Wrangler so Sharp resolves to its fixed version and
    refresh Debian runtime packages in this candidate, then rerun all validation;
    this is bounded and directly removes the observed vulnerable versions but
    adds repository maintenance to the feature revision. C repair security on a
    separate main-based change first and later integrate it; this keeps concerns
    separate but requires another branch, review, merge and integration sequence
    before PR 147 can become green.

pending U_STAGE:
  |
    No live Stage deployment or paid A3 provider smoke has run for this
    candidate. Local and CI review cannot establish those later effects.

evidence E_CORRECTION:
  |
    The bounded correction updated Hono to 4.13.7, Wrangler to 4.131.1 and its
    transitive Sharp to 0.35.4, and added a targeted Debian runtime upgrade of
    libpcre2-8-0 before the final image switches to the non-root user. npm audit then reported zero
    vulnerabilities. All 814 tests, typecheck, build, static checks and
    git diff --check passed after the correction. ADR check exited zero with the
    same legacy out-of-scope findings and clean ADR-0030 and ADR-0031 results.

pending U_REMOTE:
  |
    Docker is unavailable in the active WSL environment, so the rebuilt runtime
    package version and both revised GitHub security jobs remain unobserved until
    this local revision is committed, pushed under separate authority, and CI
    read back. The correction is not yet remote-verified.

decision D1 based_on P1, AUTHORITY, E_REVISION, E_IMPLEMENTATION, E_LOCAL, E_PR_CI, E_DRIFT, CAUSAL_CLASSIFICATION, ALTERNATIVES, E_CORRECTION, U_STAGE, U_REMOTE:
  |
    The integrated A3 and B8 implementation is review-complete with no code
    defect found in the reviewed scope. Retain the bounded dependency and runtime
    package correction as part of one local review candidate because it removes
    the observed vulnerable versions while preserving the functional boundary.
    Do not mark cc301 done and do not describe PR 147 as merge-ready until a
    pushed exact revision has passing validate, worker, security and backend-image
    checks. Merge, tag, Stage and provider effects remain separate and unperformed.
